/*
# The Guardian image (guardian/deploy/Dockerfile) COPYs the repo-root requirements.lock and
# installs it --require-hashes. `/*` above excludes every root file, so the lock has to be
# re-included by name or the build fails at `COPY requirements.lock` with "not found" (ADR-141:
# the M10 commit added the COPY but not this line, so the build broke the first time layer 10
# reached it). A file, not a directory, so no trailing slash.
!/requirements.lock
!/monitor/
!/guardian/
!/scenarios/
/scenarios/*
!/scenarios/__init__.py
!/scenarios/schemas/
/scenarios/schemas/*
!/scenarios/schemas/__init__.py
!/scenarios/schemas/yamlsubset.py
!/scenarios/cve/
/scenarios/cve/*
!/scenarios/cve/images.yaml
# The in-cluster SLO probe image (ADR-085) is built from the repo root and COPYs only the two
# modules infra.probes.slo_probe imports. Un-ignore exactly those, mirroring the scenarios/schemas
# allowlist above, so the probe build sees them without pulling the rest of infra/ (boutique,
# cilium, observability, the langfuse data volumes) into any image's context.
!/infra/
/infra/*
# ADR-182: guardian/deploy/Dockerfile reads PERL_BASE_VERSION from infra/versions.env inside the
# build, so a builder that forgets to forward a build arg cannot build a different image from the
# one the VM runs -- the failure the self-scan CI job hit when the pin first arrived as an ARG. The
# LAST matching pattern wins in a .dockerignore, so this re-inclusion has to sit after the
# `/infra/*` exclusion above rather than beside the root `requirements.lock` line.
!/infra/versions.env
!/infra/__init__.py
!/infra/probes/
/infra/probes/*
!/infra/probes/__init__.py
!/infra/probes/constants.py
!/infra/probes/slo_probe.py
monitor/.replay/
monitor/runtime/
monitor/**/__pycache__/
monitor/**/*.pyc
